{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1787082827,"nonce":"Y7tB4QvWohGbc8QGl5kPTT9YQMw=","title":"The flap detector was deleted for a blindness only a configured W can cause, and W is `NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` over a table that starts empty","was":"**What is wrong.** The flap detector was retired on ONE premise: that the case retention window W blinds `flap_score`, because a flap absorbed inside W appends neither `case.opened` nor `case.resolved` and so falls below `flap_threshold` exactly when the alert is flapping hardest. That premise is true, and it is conditional on `W \u003e 0`. **W is `NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` over a table that starts empty, and a missing row is 0.** On every deployment that has not written a `case_policy_config` row for a given `(namespace, alertname)` — which is every deployment on day one and every pair nobody has configured on every other day — nothing is absorbed, both events append normally, and the detector was correct. It was deleted anyway, and the justification never states the condition it depends on."}]}